---
import ContentPage from '../components/ContentPage.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';

const faqItems = [
  { question: 'How do I know which ingredients to use?', answer: 'Read the ingredient combination shown on the customer ticket and prepare that order using the listed items.' },
  { question: 'Where can I buy ingredients?', answer: 'Use the Grocery to restock ingredients. The Grocery and Ingredients pages list the items currently covered by this wiki.' },
  { question: 'What should I upgrade if orders are cooking too slowly?', answer: 'Compare stove tiers and consider whether a faster stove or an additional cooking station better fits your current kitchen.' },
];
---
<ContentPage title="Karinderya Recipes & Orders" description="Browse Karinderya customer orders, ingredient combinations, and cooking-system guidance." kicker="Cooking guide" intro="Use customer tickets to prepare the correct ingredient combinations." relatedLinks={[{ label: 'Food menu groups', href: '/food/' }, { label: 'Grocery', href: '/grocery/' }, { label: 'Equipment', href: '/equipment/' }]} sourceIds={['codex-menu', 'wiki-menu']} tableOfContents>
  <h2 id="recipe-system">Recipe System</h2>
  <p>Karinderya connects customer orders, ingredients, cooking equipment, and menu progression. Each customer ticket shows the items needed for that order and the displayed ticket value.</p>
  <p>Menu groups and customer-count milestones are covered on the <a href="/food/">Food page</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="how-orders-work">How Orders Work</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Read the customer ticket before preparing the order.</li>
    <li>Check that the required ingredients are available.</li>
    <li>Use an available stove to prepare the order.</li>
    <li>Serve the completed order and continue the customer flow.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="customer-orders">Customer Orders</h2>
  <p>The table shows two customer-ticket combinations and their displayed values.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Order</th><th scope="col">Displayed items</th><th scope="col">Ticket value</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><th scope="row">Order 1</th><td>1 Rice + 1 Condiments</td><td>&#8369;35</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Order 2</th><td>1 Rice + 1 Egg + 1 Condiments</td><td>&#8369;75</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>

  <h2 id="ingredient-usage">Ingredient Usage</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/ingredients/rice/">Rice</a> appears in both tickets.</li>
    <li><a href="/ingredients/condiments/">Condiments</a> appear in both tickets.</li>
    <li><a href="/ingredients/eggs/">Egg</a> appears in the second ticket.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Use the individual ingredient pages for grocery information and related order references.</p>

  <h2 id="using-the-order-list">Using the Order List</h2>
  <p>Read each row as a customer ticket: the middle column shows the ingredient combination, and the value column shows the ticket total. Match the displayed items instead of relying on the order value alone.</p>

  <h2 id="cooking-tips">Cooking Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Restock frequently used ingredients before accepting a busy queue of orders.</li>
    <li>Read the full ticket so similar orders are not confused.</li>
    <li>Keep an available stove ready when several customers are waiting.</li>
    <li>Use the Food page to review menu groups and progression milestones.</li>
  </ul>

  <FAQ items={faqItems} />
</ContentPage>
